LATEST IMPLEMENTATION — MB-02B
mirror_state::v2 now provides LedgerV2, StagedLedgerV2, AccountV2 and typed ledger/
operation errors. Fields are private; callers cannot install an arbitrary account
map or membership cache. Bootstrap accepts VerifiedBootstrap and exact configured
synthetic allocations; no implicit founder, seed or marketing account is funded.
Both wrappers expose readonly account/config/membership/height views, account_bytes,
accounts_root, economics_root and combined root. Ledger also exposes external tip.

LedgerV2::stage_operations takes a stable trusted ParentChainViewV2 and the complete
ordered SignedOperationV2 list. Shared core validate_operation_limits_v2 preflights
full counts, individual sizes, enrollment/member quotas and block bytes before
projection allocation, candidate clones or signature work. Personhood then validates
exact parent configuration/height/hash and checked next height, snapshots parent
Active keys and expires Pending entries. Accounts clone only after parent binding.

Execute every transfer/member operation in original full order. Earlier failures
win over later operation failures; structural/parent errors precede that loop.
The candidate is local and discarded on any failure. Membership finalizes only at
block end, then account invariants are checked before returning both components.
Late transfer failure rolls back earlier membership and vice versa, including
expiry. The immutable parent is unchanged on success too. Empty bodies still
advance height and process pending expiry.

Transfers require signed context/window/canonical-anchor authorization, positive
amount, fee0, exact account sequence with checked increment, sufficient funds,
checked recipient credit and account capacity. Funded self-transfers advance one
account sequence without changing money. Explicit zero allocations and spent
zero-balance accounts remain present, preserving nonce/capacity history. Missing
accounts read as zero but contains_account distinguishes absence. Receiving funds
may create an account. Account/member sequences stay separate; membership status
adds no new spending restriction. Sum balances equals initial synthetic supply.
There is NO mint, fee redistribution, grant, population payout or reward API.

MembershipRegistryV2::begin_indexed_block(parent,total_count,indexed_operations)
returns opaque IndexedMembershipStageV2. It owns no public partial-state accessor,
Clone or registry conversion. apply_next(self,expected_full_index) consumes it;
a failed operation cannot be skipped and the old builder reused. finish(self)
requires the entire planned membership sequence before activation/invariants.
Indices are strictly increasing and below total_count. Omitted transfers are
charged EXACTLY (4+243) bytes each plus168 block overhead and actual member sizes.
Core checks the actual full list separately. New omitted kinds/lengths require
explicit review of this cross-crate contract. Existing membership-only stage_block
uses shared machinery through a borrowed contiguous plan, preserving old vectors.

MPS2 INDEX COMPATIBILITY EXTENSION
Runtime enrollment positions now require index < max_operations; the membership-
operation count cap is not a full-block position bound. This explicit accepted-
range extension changes no serialized field/domain. Older decoders can reject new
mixed positions. A decoded MPS2 remains an untrusted wrapper with no runtime-state
conversion. MPH2 remains membership-only with its old bytes/budgets; it rejects
transfers. Never drop transfers to feed a mixed history into MPH2/stage_block.

FROZEN LEDGER ROOT BYTES
All integers unsigned little-endian, addresses/hashes raw32 bytes, exact ASCII
domains without NUL. H=SHA256d. Account payload = u32 count + raw-byte-sorted
(address32,balanceu64,next_account_sequenceu64) records,48 bytes each, including
explicit zeros and exhausted accounts. Accounts root domain MIRROR_ACCOUNTS_V2.
Membership root remains H(MIRROR_MEMBERSHIP_STATE_V2 || exact MPS2 bytes).
Economics root = H(MIRROR_ECONOMICS_DISABLED_V2 || initial_test_supplyu64).
Ledger root = H(MIRROR_LEDGER_STATE_V2 || C32 || heightu64 || accounts_root32 ||
membership_root32 || economics_root32),136 payload bytes. Height/C come from
membership; no second divergent account height. Current block hash is excluded
to avoid a circular header/root commitment. See docs/LEDGER_STATE_V2.md.

